msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Bayesian Sampling supports Bayesian planning and inference for acceptance "
"sampling with a Beta prior on the lot proportion defective. The procedure "
"text describes the hypotheses and workflow. Planning finds candidate "
"sampling plans; inference updates the selected prior using the observed "
"sample and predicts defects in the lot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Numerical Details"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Bayes factors are calculated from log probabilities without clipping the "
"hypothesis-region probabilities. Planning, acceptance numbers and evidence "
"labels use these log-scale values. Differences within a small floating-point "
"round-off allowance are treated as ties, so a numerical tie meets the "
"selected target. Very large or small Bayes factors are displayed in "
"scientific notation; displayed region probabilities may round to 0 or 1 "
"without affecting the Bayes-factor calculation."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"For the two-region impartial prior, calibration checks the returned Beta "
"parameters: the selected shape must hold strictly, and the location and "
"probability below RQL must match their requested values within an absolute "
"error of 1e-8. A failure is reported rather than using an approximate prior "
"outside that tolerance."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"For the three-region impartial prior, two nested root searches match the "
"cumulative probabilities at AQL and RQL to 1/3 and 2/3. All three resulting "
"region probabilities must be within an absolute error of 1e-8 of 1/3. This "
"is a numerical accuracy check, not a statistical uncertainty interval. The "
"search has no fixed upper bound on the Beta parameters; very close quality "
"limits can imply a highly concentrated prior. If numerical accuracy cannot "
"be verified, an explicit calibration error is shown. Shape boundaries at "
"alpha = 1 or beta = 1 are allowed only when the resulting prior also passes "
"the same probability checks."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Beta-binomial count probabilities are evaluated using adjacent-count ratios "
"and normalized over their full support. This avoids loss of precision for "
"highly concentrated priors without changing the posterior predictive model."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Choose the quality limits, prior distribution, maximum sample size and "
"minimum Bayes-factor target. In the standard two-hypothesis workflow, "
"planning targets evidence about whether the lot proportion defective is "
"below the RQL."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Quality Levels"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Acceptable quality level (AQL)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Acceptable quality level (AQL), expressed as a proportion defective between "
"0 and 1."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"For the default unimodal two-hypothesis impartial prior, AQL sets the mode "
"(peak) unless a custom mode is specified. The prior assigns 50% probability "
"below RQL and 50% above it. For a U-shaped impartial prior, AQL instead sets "
"the interior minimum unless a custom minimum is specified. In the three-"
"hypothesis workflow, AQL separates the Good and Middle regions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Rejectable quality level (RQL or LTPD)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Proportion-defective threshold for unacceptable quality and the main "
"threshold used in two-hypothesis planning and inference."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Also called the lot tolerance percent defective (LTPD). Enter a proportion "
"between 0 and 1 (for example, 0.10 means 10%)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Beta Prior"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Select a Beta prior for the lot proportion defective. The selected prior is "
"used for both planning and inference."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Impartial (two-region)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Assigns 50% prior probability below RQL and 50% above it. Choose a unimodal "
"prior with an interior peak or a U-shaped prior with an interior minimum "
"between the endpoint peaks. The location defaults to AQL. Incompatible "
"combinations produce an error; the analysis does not automatically change "
"the shape, location or probability split."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Two-region prior shape"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Both shapes assign half of the prior probability below RQL. For Unimodal "
"(the default), the location is the peak and RQL must lie strictly between "
"that mode and 0.5. For U-shaped, the location is the interior minimum and "
"the minimum and RQL must lie on opposite sides of 0.5. Both the location and "
"RQL must be strictly between 0 and 1."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"A location and RQL both equal to 0.5 leave infinitely many priors of either "
"shape possible. Choose Custom to specify the desired parameters."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Unimodal"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "U-shaped"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Custom minimum"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Custom mode"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Two-region custom location"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"When unchecked, AQL is used as the location. Changing shape retains the "
"location; incompatible combinations show an error."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Prior location"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "(default: AQL)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Location of the interior peak for Unimodal or the interior minimum for U-"
"shaped, between 0 and 1. Switching shape retains this value."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Impartial (three-region)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Assigns one third of the prior probability to each of Good (below AQL), "
"Middle (between AQL and RQL), and Bad (above RQL). The limits must satisfy 0 "
"< AQL < RQL < 1."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Three-region shape constraint"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Any shape (the default) applies no additional shape restriction. "
"Alternatively, exclude U-shapes (alpha >= 1 or beta >= 1), or require both "
"parameters to be at least 1. The equal-thirds prior must satisfy the "
"selected constraint. Incompatible quality limits and shape constraints "
"produce an error. Change the limits or constraint; the probability split is "
"not changed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Uses the equal-thirds Beta prior without additional shape restrictions."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Requires at least one of alpha or beta to be at least 1, allowing monotone "
"priors but excluding U-shaped priors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Requires both alpha and beta to be at least 1, also excluding monotone "
"priors that have either parameter below 1."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Any shape"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Exclude U-shaped"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "α ≥ 1 and β ≥ 1"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Uses a Beta(1, 1) prior."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Specify the two positive shape parameters of the Beta prior."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "First shape parameter (alpha) of the custom Beta prior."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Second shape parameter (beta) of the custom Beta prior."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Planning Criteria"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "(Max) sample size (n)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Maximum sample size searched when finding candidate sampling plans."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Minimum target Bayes factor in favor of a proportion defective below the "
"RQL. This target is used for planning and for the acceptance number and "
"target status reported under Inference. Equality meets the target; not "
"reaching it does not by itself imply rejection. A target at or below 1 can "
"be reached without evidence favoring a proportion defective below the RQL."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Plan table"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Show candidate sampling plans meeting the selected minimum Bayes-factor "
"target within the maximum sample size."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Plot the selected Beta prior. The plot remains available even if the sample-"
"size limit and Bayes-factor target yield no feasible plan. Adaptive grids "
"resolve narrow peaks and both tails. If the density diverges at 0 or 1, its "
"curve continues beyond the finite vertical display range; this affects only "
"the display, not probabilities or Bayes factors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Show Bayes-factor comparisons for the Good, Middle and Bad regions defined "
"by AQL and RQL."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Use the selected prior and observed sample to compute the posterior "
"distribution, Bayes-factor evidence and posterior predictive lot-quality "
"probabilities. Invalid sample counts, lot sizes or Bayes-factor targets "
"produce an explanatory error; correcting the inputs restores the results."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Posterior distribution"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Update the selected Beta prior using the sample size n and observed "
"defectives d. Counts must satisfy 0 <= d <= n <= N. The input fields retain "
"inconsistent counts so that the analysis can explain the problem. If d "
"exceeds n or n exceeds N, correct whichever entry was mistaken; dependent "
"inference results return after the inputs are valid."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Number of inspected items in the sample. This must not exceed the lot size."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid "Observed number of defectives (d)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Number of defective items observed in the inspected sample. This must not "
"exceed the sample size."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Total number of items in the lot, including inspected and uninspected items."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Show posterior Bayes-factor evidence and target status. Evidence labels "
"describe support for a proportion defective below versus at or above the "
"RQL; whether the selected target is reached is reported separately. Both use "
"the unrounded Bayes factor. The acceptance number c is the largest observed "
"defect count at the specified inference sample size that meets the target. "
"\"Not available\" means that no count meets it at that sample size."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Plot the updated Beta posterior and its Bayes-factor evidence and target "
"status. Adaptive grids resolve narrow peaks and both tails. If the density "
"diverges at 0 or 1, its curve continues beyond the finite vertical display "
"range; this affects only the display, not probabilities or Bayes factors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSampling|"
msgid ""
"Plot the posterior predictive distribution of lot-level defectives, "
"conditional on the observed sample data."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"*Bayesian State-Space Sampling* performs acceptance sampling with a Bayesian "
"state-space model for defect rates over lots."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Data Requirements"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Use one row per lot. Rows are sorted by Lot Number, and the current lot is "
"the one with the largest number. Duplicate lot numbers are rejected. If "
"further items from the same lot are inspected, update its existing Sample "
"Size and Defect Count rather than appending another cumulative-inspection "
"row."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Lot numbers determine order only. Their spacing does not change the state-"
"transition variance: lots numbered 1, 2, 3 and lots numbered 1, 10, 100 have "
"the same model transitions when their data are otherwise identical."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Defect Count, Sample Size and Lot Size must be finite, nonnegative whole "
"numbers, with Defect Count ≤ Sample Size ≤ Lot Size. Fractional values are "
"rejected rather than truncated; counts must be smaller than 2,147,483,647 to "
"fit the implementation's integer indexing. Zero inspected items, zero "
"observed defects, all inspected items defective, and full inspection are "
"supported. A zero-size lot is allowed only with zero inspected items and "
"zero observed defects; it still occupies a position in the state sequence. A "
"single lot is supported without a predictor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Every assigned column must be complete. A missing or non-finite value in Lot "
"Number, Defect Count, Sample Size, Lot Size, or an assigned covariate stops "
"the analysis with an error naming the affected field; no acceptance decision "
"is produced. Lots are not automatically dropped, and missing values are "
"neither imputed nor treated as zero. Unassigned columns do not affect the "
"analysis. For a genuinely uninspected lot, enter Sample Size = 0 and Defect "
"Count = 0; do not replace an unknown count from an inspected sample with "
"zero."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"With covariates, at least two lots are required, and every selected "
"covariate must contain varying, finite numeric values. Each covariate is "
"centered at its own mean and divided by its own sample standard deviation "
"over all supplied rows, without weighting by sample size. Appending lots can "
"change this scaling and hence the meaning of a one-SD effect. The Model "
"section explains the coefficients and their priors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The analysis rejects linearly dependent covariates, such as duplicate "
"variables or a variable that is an exact linear combination of the others "
"after centering. Remove redundant covariates before fitting. Strongly "
"correlated covariates can still be difficult to distinguish, and covariates "
"that track time can be difficult to distinguish from changes in the latent "
"baseline. For short series, use a small number of covariates with a clear "
"substantive purpose."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Updating Data and Refitting"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Each fit uses all supplied lots jointly. To inspect more items from the "
"current lot, update its cumulative Sample Size and Defect Count in the "
"existing row and rerun the analysis. Append a row only for a new lot. The "
"interface does not automatically inspect items or run an item-by-item "
"optional-stopping loop."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Changing the supplied data, covariate assignments, priors or MCMC settings "
"requires a new fit of the supplied series. Changing quality limits, decision "
"thresholds or displayed outputs reuses the fitted posterior samples; it does "
"not change the model posterior."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Output"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"- **Posterior Summary (Current Lot)**: observed defects, posterior "
"predictive summary, and acceptance decision. A decision-specific note "
"explains the proposal using the selected probability thresholds; the "
"calculated probabilities remain in the table.\n"
"- **Predictor Coefficients** (automatically shown when covariates are "
"included): posterior mean, median, and equal-tailed 95% credible interval "
"(2.5th and 97.5th percentiles) for each coefficient. These describe changes "
"in the log-odds of a defect per one SD increase in the covariate, holding "
"the latent baseline and other covariates fixed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Observed defects in each sampled lot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Sample Size (Tested Items)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Number of tested items per lot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Lot Size (Total Items)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Total items per lot."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Unique numeric sequence/order index for each lot, with measurement type "
"**Scale** or **Ordinal**. Ordinal columns must have numeric labels; their "
"numeric values determine the order, regardless of category-level order. "
"Ordered text labels are not supported."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Covariates (Optional)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Assign one or more numeric covariates to include their additive effects in "
"the model. Leave this field empty to fit the model without predictors. "
"Adding or removing a covariate refits the model. The common coefficient "
"prior scale can be set under Model before assigning covariates; coefficient "
"plots and diagnostic controls are shown when covariates are assigned. "
"Categorical predictors and interaction terms are not supported."
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"AQL and RQL are defect **proportions**, entered between 0 and 1. For "
"example, an AQL of 0.025 corresponds to 25 defects in a lot of size 1,000. "
"Let %1 be the total number of defects in the current lot, %2 its size, and "
"%3 all supplied observations. The decision uses the posterior predictive "
"probabilities"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Let a be the **Acceptance threshold** (default 0.10) and r the **Rejection "
"threshold** (default 0.05). The result is:"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"- **Consider to Accept** if H &lt; a.\n"
"- **Consider to Reject** if H &gt; a and L &lt; r.\n"
"- **Consider to Continue** otherwise."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The fields beside **Accept if** and **Reject if** set a and r, respectively. "
"The rejection label also displays the current value of a, so both required "
"conditions are visible."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"All inequalities are strict. In particular, H = a gives Continue. Counts "
"exactly at a quality limit are excluded from its corresponding strict tail. "
"Products within floating-point precision of an integer are treated as that "
"integer; genuinely fractional count limits are not rounded. These "
"probabilities concern the total defects in the finite lot, including "
"observed and uninspected items, rather than the latent defect probability "
"alone. The count-based expressions also apply to a zero-size lot, for which "
"a defect proportion is undefined."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The thresholds express model-based posterior decision criteria. They do not "
"by themselves guarantee frequentist producer's or consumer's error rates "
"across repeated samples."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Quality Levels"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Acceptable quality level (AQL)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Acceptable quality level (AQL), expressed as a proportion defective between "
"0 and 1."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Rejectable quality level (RQL or LTPD)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Rejectable quality level (RQL), also called the lot tolerance percent "
"defective (LTPD). Enter a proportion between 0 and 1 (for example, 0.10 "
"means 10%)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Accept if P(above RQL) <"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Acceptance threshold a (default 0.10). Consider to Accept when H &lt; a, "
"where H is the posterior predictive probability that the total defects in "
"the current lot exceed RQL times its size."
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Reject if P(above RQL) > %1 and P(below AQL) <"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Rejection threshold r (default 0.05). Consider to Reject when H &gt; a and L "
"&lt; r, where H is the posterior predictive probability that total defects "
"exceed RQL times the lot size and L is the probability that they are below "
"AQL times the lot size. Equality to the acceptance threshold gives Continue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Continue sampling if neither rule is satisfied."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Reading the State Trajectory"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The trajectory shows the lot-specific defect probabilities, including any "
"covariate contributions. It conditions on all supplied observations. "
"Estimates for earlier lots therefore use later supplied observations as "
"well: this is **smoothing**. They can change when more lots are added and "
"should not be read as the estimates or decisions that would have been "
"available when each earlier lot was inspected. The current lot is the last "
"lot in the supplied sequence; its prediction uses observations available in "
"that dataset."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Prediction for the Current Lot"
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"For current lot %1, with %2 total items, %3 inspected and %4 observed "
"defects, the model predicts the remaining defects %5 and total %6 as"
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The posterior predictive distribution averages this conditional distribution "
"over the posterior uncertainty in %1. It combines uncertainty about the "
"defect probability with binomial variability among the uninspected items."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The predictive plot displays approximately the central 99.8% range (0.1st–"
"99.9th percentiles), expanded to include AQL/RQL count limits and rounded "
"axis limits. Very small tails may fall outside the displayed range. The bins "
"contain equal numbers of whole defect counts, with one bar per count for "
"short ranges. Bars show the probability mass in each bin and are **not "
"renormalized** after selecting the display range. The summary probabilities "
"and decision always use the full predictive distribution, including any "
"undisplayed tails."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Valid predictions range from the observed defect count to that count plus "
"the number of uninspected items; a fully inspected lot has probability one "
"at its observed total. If predictive draws are missing, non-finite, "
"noninteger or outside this range, or their probabilities do not sum to one, "
"the analysis reports an error instead of an acceptance decision. A divergent "
"transition alone does not make a predictive draw invalid; these draws are "
"retained and their computational warnings should be investigated."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Predictor Coefficient Plots"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The coefficient density plots use all posterior draws and extend beyond the "
"sampled range so that the tails approach zero. The default axes also include "
"zero as a reference. Adjusting the axes changes the display, not the "
"posterior draws or coefficient summaries. With weakly identified effects, "
"Cauchy tails can make coefficient means and SDs unstable or undefined. "
"Inspect the computational diagnostics and assess prior sensitivity before "
"interpreting such summaries."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Defect-rate state trajectory over lots: posterior means with pointwise 95% "
"credible intervals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Posterior predictive distribution of total defects in the current lot: "
"observed defects plus predicted defects among its uninspected items. It "
"cannot contain fewer defects than already observed; after inspecting the "
"entire lot, its total defect count is known."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Posterior distribution of latest defect rate."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Posteriors for predictor coefficients"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Posterior distributions of predictor coefficients, labeled by covariate."
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"For lot %1, let %2 be its observed defects, %3 its inspected items and %4 "
"its latent defect probability. The observation model is"
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Let %1 denote the initial baseline probability (the %2 prior controls in the "
"interface) and %3 the baseline log odds. Across lots,"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "with innovations"
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The second argument of %1 is its variance. The regular component has SD %2, "
"the **baseline innovation scale** estimated from the data. The broad "
"component has SD %3 and accommodates larger changes. Both are centered at "
"zero, allowing quality to improve or deteriorate. The baseline scale is not "
"the SD of the entire mixture."
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The mixture weight %1 and additional spread %2 are fixed model settings; %2 "
"is on the logit scale. Conditional on the shared baseline scale, innovations "
"are independent draws from this mixture. A particular transition can receive "
"stronger posterior support for the broad component, but the shared prior "
"weight stays at 0.05. The model does not estimate probabilities of switching "
"between persistent regimes."
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Without predictors, %1. With %2 numeric covariates,"
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"where %1 is covariate %2's sample SD over the supplied lots and each "
"coefficient %3 is shared across lots. Equivalently, the vector of log odds "
"is %4, where %5 contains the standardized covariate columns. No additional "
"intercept is included because the latent baseline already supplies it."
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"A one-SD increase in covariate %1 changes the log odds by %2, holding the "
"other covariates and the baseline fixed; it multiplies the odds by %3. In "
"this mode, %4 is the first lot's baseline probability when all covariates "
"are at their means, and its actual defect probability also includes the "
"combined covariate contribution."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Priors"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The following priors are independent. Their hyperparameters are adjustable "
"in the Model section."
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"| Parameter | Prior | Default settings |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Initial baseline probability %1 | Beta | Shape parameters 1 and 1 "
"(uniform) |\n"
"| Baseline innovation scale %2 | Half-normal | Scale 1 |\n"
"| Each predictor coefficient %3 | Independent Cauchy, centered at zero | "
"Common scale 0.707 |"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Adding covariates can broaden the prior on their combined contribution to "
"the log odds even when the individual coefficient scale stays unchanged. The "
"model does not automatically increase shrinkage as more covariates are "
"added. Choose covariates and priors using relevant process knowledge and "
"assess sensitivity when the series is short or effects are weakly identified."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Initial Baseline Probability"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Beta prior for the first lot's defect probability without predictors, or its "
"baseline probability when all covariates are at their means."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"First shape parameter of the beta prior for the initial baseline "
"probability. The default shape parameters are 1 and 1, giving a uniform "
"prior."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Second shape parameter of the beta prior for the initial baseline "
"probability. The default shape parameters are 1 and 1, giving a uniform "
"prior."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Baseline Innovation Scale"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Half-normal prior scale"
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The **Half-normal prior scale** is the SD of the underlying zero-centered "
"normal distribution before restricting it to positive values; it is not the "
"SD of the resulting half-normal distribution. This control sets the width of "
"the prior for %1, which is estimated from the data. The half-normal prior "
"favors smaller baseline scales while allowing larger values."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Predictor Coefficients"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Common scale of the independent zero-centered Cauchy priors for the "
"predictor coefficients. You can set this before assigning covariates. Each "
"coefficient is the change in log odds per one standard deviation increase in "
"that covariate, holding the other covariates and baseline fixed."
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The **Cauchy scale** control applies separately to every coefficient; the "
"coefficients are not constrained to be equal. Each prior is expressed per "
"one SD of its covariate. In original covariate units, the coefficient is %1, "
"and its prior scale is the chosen Cauchy scale divided by %2. Because "
"covariates are standardized over the supplied dataset at each fit, appending "
"lots can change these original-unit priors."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Check computational diagnostics before interpreting the results. Select "
"**MCMC Diagnostics → Diagnostic report** to see the full report. The checks "
"run even when this option is off, and any warnings remain visible alongside "
"the results. All retained post-warmup draws are used, including those "
"associated with divergent transitions. Warnings qualify the posterior "
"summaries and decisions; they do not remove draws or suppress these outputs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The checks assess all sampled parameters: the initial baseline log odds "
"(`mu1`), baseline innovation scale, variables used to construct the "
"innovations (`z_raw`), and every predictor coefficient when present. They "
"report divergences, maximum-treedepth hits, rank-normalized split R-hat (the "
"maximum of its folded and unfolded versions), bulk ESS, tail ESS, and per-"
"chain E-BFMI. RStan's `Rhat()`, `ess_bulk()` and `ess_tail()` functions "
"calculate the mixing diagnostics from iteration-ordered chains. E-BFMI is "
"`mean(diff(energy)^2) / var(energy)`, calculated separately for each chain."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Warnings flag any retained divergence or treedepth hit, R-hat at or above "
"1.01, bulk or tail ESS below 100 times the number of chains, and E-BFMI "
"below 0.3. These are screening thresholds, not guarantees of convergence. "
"Divergences and poor mixing can compromise estimates; treedepth saturation "
"can reduce efficiency. See [Stan's diagnostic guidance](https://mc-stan.org/"
"learn-stan/diagnostics-warnings.html) for investigation and remedies."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"A single chain cannot establish between-chain agreement, so the rank-"
"normalized split R-hat check is unavailable. At least six retained draws per "
"chain are required before computing the mixing diagnostics; this is only a "
"computational minimum. Constant or non-finite sampled-parameter chains and "
"missing diagnostics trigger explicit qualifications. Constant generated "
"quantities, such as a known total after complete inspection, do not by "
"themselves indicate sampler failure. Unavailable checks should not be "
"interpreted as evidence of convergence."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Diagnostic report"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Show sampler and convergence checks for all sampled parameters."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"Under **MCMC Diagnostics**, **Diagnostic report** displays the full "
"computational diagnostic report and is off by default. The checks always "
"run, and warnings about problems or unavailable checks are shown regardless "
"of this option. **Overview table** separately displays posterior summaries "
"and traditional MCMC diagnostics for the selected parameters."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid "Show the mean, SD, ESS, and R-hat for the selected parameters."
msgstr ""

#, qt-format
msgctxt "BayesianSSMforAS|"
msgid ""
"The **Overview table** summarizes the parameters selected below it. **Sigma "
"(state noise)** refers to the baseline innovation scale %1. This table's ESS "
"(`n_eff`) and R-hat columns use RStan's traditional raw-draw ESS and "
"unranked split R-hat, which differ from the rank-based diagnostics in the "
"full computational report. Undefined diagnostics for constant generated "
"quantities should not be read as successful convergence checks."
msgstr ""

